Sval: Firefox's shortcut editor's actor serves Settings

Settings' Keyboard shortcuts pane (Sval's `settings-keyboard.js`) lists and
changes keys through Firefox's own `CustomKeys` actor, which lists the
window's keys, remaps them in `CustomKeys` and captures the new keystroke on
the page's `<browser>`. about:preferences loads in the parent process, so the
actor matches it there. Sval does not build about:keyboard
(`no-closed-about-pages.patch`), so the actor needs no page of its own. Registering the actor afresh from
Sval's code would have to unregister Mozilla's after DesktopActorRegistry
has made it, a second declaration of the same actor.

diff --git a/browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs b/browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs
index 0c863af656..9856351023 100644
--- a/browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs
+++ b/browser/components/DesktopActorRegistry.sys.mjs
@@ -438,8 +438,10 @@ let JSWINDOWACTORS = {
         DOMDocElementInserted: { wantUntrusted: true },
       },
     },
-    matches: ["about:keyboard"],
-    remoteTypes: ["privilegedabout"],
+    // Sval: Settings' Keyboard shortcuts pane takes about:keyboard's place.
+    includeChrome: true,
+    matches: ["about:preferences*", "about:settings*"],
+    remoteTypes: ["parent"],
   },
 
